---
import {CaseSensitive, Brain, Image} from '@lucide/astro'
---

<section class="flex flex-col items-center gap-8">
    <div class="w-full gap-4 flex flex-col items-center text-center">
        <h2 class="text-white text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold uppercase">how does it work?</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-paragraph text-md md:text-lg tracking-wide">
            This is how our meme generation process works, simplified:
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row w-full gap-8">
        <section class="min-h-[10rem] w-full bg-black/20 rounded-2xl p-6 px-12 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4">
            <CaseSensitive class="w-12 h-12 text-magenta-500" />
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold uppercase">Step 1</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-paragraph text-center">Bot chooses a template based on like/dislike metrics, picks 10-15 messages and an image (or a GIF).</p>
        </section>
        <section class="min-h-[10rem] w-full bg-black/20 rounded-2xl p-6 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4">
            <Brain class="w-12 h-12 text-magenta-500" />
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold uppercase">Step 2</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-paragraph text-center">Chosen meme engine "transforms" given messages into meme text so that they fit the template.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="min-h-[10rem] w-full bg-black/20 rounded-2xl p-6 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4">
            <Image class="w-12 h-12 text-magenta-500" />
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold uppercase">Step 3</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-paragraph text-center">Text and an image get applied onto a meme template, which then sent to the user who requested it</p>
        </section>
    </div>
</section>